{
  "about": "A block's document (docs/dev/documents.md): one property, doc = {format, name, hash, ext, at, url?, size?, copy?}, in that key order; at is store, path, url or listed (a work folder's file too large to keep: no hash, no address, its size, never a PDF or a Markdown file). cases: gamma/documents/model.py page_document and frontend/src/documents/pageDocument.js pageDocument, properties in, the view out ({format, language, name, hash, ext, size, at, url, file, copy}: url is where the document is fetched from, the address for at url, else /api/uploads/<file>, '' for a listed file; file is hash + ext, '' without a hash; language is a text document's), null for no doc or one that does not check (gamma/documents/model.py check_document). legacy: the backend alone, step 52's rewrite of the flat keys doc_id, source_url (sourceUrl), original_filename and linked_file (gamma/normalize.py document_shape): properties is a row's before, migrated after. copies: the client alone, the doc a duplicated page stores (copyDocument of the page's view), in the canonical form check_document leaves it in (an address that is exactly an upload's is a copy of that upload), null when the page has none. Read by backend/tests/test_shared_fixtures.py, backend/tests/test_migrations.py, frontend/tests/documents.test.mjs and frontend/tests/viewers.test.mjs (the code view's language of an opened Markdown file).",
